{"episodes":{"208435":"A fast-moving Quasi-Linear Convective System (QLCS) in an anomalously warm and humid mid-winter environment led to an uncommon tornado outbreak on December 28, 2025. Over a dozen mainly-weak tornadoes occurred from central Illinois to the Ohio Valley. One brief tornado occurred in central Indiana in the town of Linton. Damaging straight-line winds were also reported in several locations across central Indiana. The tornado path was surveyed by NWS Indianapolis on Monday, December 29, 2025, and determined to be of EF-1 intensity with estimated peak winds of 100 MPH.","208437":"A narrow line of thunderstorms moved through the area during the evening hours.","208438":"A narrow line of thunderstorms moved through the area during the evening hours.","208439":"A narrow line of thunderstorms moved through the area during the evening hours.","208513":"High winds developed over southern Lake Michigan during the early morning hours of December 29th.","208516":"A cold front moving through Middle Tennessee during the evening of December 28, 2025, brought a line of showers and thunderstorms into the area. Gusty winds were associated with this activity, and while they generally remained sub-severe, a couple trees were reported down in the Springfield area.","209222":"West-northwesterly winds become gusty behind a cold front crossing the York and James Rivers on December 29.","209667":"A strong winter storm moved through the Upper Great Lakes bringing high end gales and storm force winds.","209668":"A strong winter storm moved through the Upper Great Lakes bringing high end gales and storm force winds.","209783":"During the evening hours on December 28th, a strong cold front moved across the Ohio Valley, bringing a line of showers and thunderstorms through the region ahead of the front. Before the front passed through, temperatures were able to warm into the 70s during the day on December 28th, with southerly flow also helping to increase moisture as dewpoint temperatures rose into the upper 50s and low 60s. As the line of storms began to push across southern Indiana, the instability began to greatly decrease as the line pushed from west to east across the area. Still, there was enough instability to sustain storms across much of the area, with scattered wind damage and strong wind gusts observed. One spin-up EF0 tornado occurred in southern Harrison County near the Central community, with maximum wind speeds estimated around 75 to 80 mph.","209820":"During the evening hours on December 28th, a strong cold front moved across the Ohio Valley, bringing a line of showers and thunderstorms through the region ahead of the front. Before the front passed through, temperatures were able to warm into the 70s during the day on December 28th, with southerly flow also helping to increase moisture as dewpoint temperatures rose into the upper 50s and low 60s. As the line of storms began to push across southern Indiana and central Kentucky, the instability began to greatly decrease as the line pushed from west to east across the area. Still, there was enough instability to sustain storms across much of the area, with scattered wind damage and strong wind gusts observed."},"events":[{"begin":"2025-12-29T00:18Z","county":"Knox","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"4.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2025-12-29T00:18Z","endLat":38.68,"endLon":-87.47,"episode":208435,"id":1300082,"injuries":0,"lat":38.68,"location":"2.7 W Fritchton","lon":-87.47,"magnitude":52.0,"magnitudeType":"EG","narrative":"Thunderstorm wind gusts downed multiple trees.","source":"Emergency Manager","state":"IN","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"IND"},{"begin":"2025-12-29T00:18Z","county":"Greene","damageProperty":"1.50M","deaths":0,"end":"2025-12-29T00:20Z","endLat":39.04,"endLon":-87.15,"episode":208435,"id":1304534,"injuries":1,"lat":39.03,"location":"Linton","lon":-87.17,"narrative":"A line of strong to severe storms moved across central and southern Indiana during the evening. As the line of storms approached Greene County a surge or bowing segment was noted in the line. This allowed for a quick moving tornado to impact downtown Linton. The tornado started near the corner of A Street SW and 6th Street SW and moved northeast through downtown Linton. The strongest damage was noted along Main St between West Vincennes St and A Street SW. This is where damage consistent with an EF1 tornado had occurred.  This caused damage to roofs of masonry buildings in downtown Linton. Splatter of dirt and mud in a manner consistent with a tornado was found. The tornado continued to move east-northeast doing damage between A Street NE and East Vincennes Street. Additional roof damage and tree damage was found along the path. The tornado eventually weakened and lifted shortly after moving past 12th Street NE.  Maximum winds were estimated at 100 mph.","source":"NWS Storm Survey","state":"IN","torLengthMi":1.12,"torScale":"EF1","torWidthYd":75.0,"type":"Tornado","wfo":"IND"},{"begin":"2025-12-29T00:21Z","county":"Hendricks","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"2.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2025-12-29T00:21Z","endLat":39.87,"endLon":-86.39,"episode":208435,"id":1300097,"injuries":0,"lat":39.87,"location":"1.48 NNE Brownsburg","lon":-86.39,"magnitude":52.0,"magnitudeType":"EG","narrative":"Thunderstorm wind gusts downed a large tree.","source":"Public","state":"IN","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"IND"},{"begin":"2025-12-29T00:31Z","county":"Owen","deaths":0,"end":"2025-12-29T00:31Z","endLat":39.3,"endLon":-86.75,"episode":208435,"id":1300106,"injuries":0,"lat":39.3,"location":"1.75 NE Spencer","lon":-86.75,"magnitude":53.0,"magnitudeType":"MG","narrative":"A 61 mph thunderstorm wind gust was measured by the public.","source":"Public","state":"IN","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"IND"},{"begin":"2025-12-29T00:40Z","county":"Marion","deaths":0,"end":"2025-12-29T00:40Z","endLat":39.7,"endLon":-86.26,"episode":208435,"id":1300115,"injuries":0,"lat":39.7,"